      "title": "Shell command built from upload name",
      "description": "make_thumbnail puts upload_name from the upload form into a shell string on line 8. Line 9 then runs that string with shell=True. A user who uploads a name like a.png;rm -rf ~ can run any command as the service user. A name with ../ can also read or write files outside the upload folders. Pass an argument list without shell=True. Reject names that are not a plain basename.",
      "suggested_change": "    subprocess.run([\"convert\", f\"{UPLOAD_DIR}/{upload_name}\", \"-resize\", \"128x128\", f\"{THUMB_DIR}/{upload_name}\"], check=True)",
